  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">German Marshall Fund (GMF) Minskad Polarisering 2020-2021</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">German Marshall Fund (GMF) Mitigating Polarization 2020-2021</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">The German Marshall Fund of the United States (GMF) har ans&#xf6;kt till Sida om finansiering p&#xe5; 3,65 miljoner SEK f&#xf6;r att genomf&#xf6;ra insatsen &quot;Strategies and Tools for Mitigating Polarization in Turkey&quot; under &#xe5;ren 2020 - 2021. 

Insatsen syftar till att skapa en djupare f&#xf6;rst&#xe5;else f&#xf6;r vad som ligger till grund f&#xf6;r polarisering, s&#xe4;rskilt i Turkiet, att utveckla strategier f&#xf6;r att motverka polarisering och till att f&#xf6;rse civilsamh&#xe4;llesorganisationer, politiska partier, media, utbildningsinstitutioner och andra intressenter med innovativa verktyg som de kan anv&#xe4;nda f&#xf6;r att &#xf6;vervinna polarisering.

Insatsens totala finansiering &#xe4;r 3,65 miljoner SEK och Sida &#xe4;r ensam finansi&#xe4;r.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The German Marshall Fund of the United States has applied to Sida for funding of 3,65 million SEK to carry out the intervention &quot;Strategies and Tools for Mitigating Polarization in Turkey&quot; during the period 2020 - 2021.

The intervention aims to create a deeper understanding on the sources of polarization particularly in Turkey, develop strategies for mitigating polarization and provide civil society organizations, political parties, media, educational instutions and other stakeholders with innovative tools they could use to overome polarization.

The intervention&#x2019;s total budget is 3,65 million SEK, and Sida is the only funder.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project aims to create a deeper understanding on the sources of polarization particularly in Turkey, develop strategies for mitigating polarization and provide civil society organizations, political parties, media, educational institutions and other stakeholders with innovative tools they could use to overcome polarization.</narrative>
  </description>
